e middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and October to November and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 173% of normal in April to May and 37% in July to August. So far in 2026 it sat at 38% in January to February and 122% in June to July. Every grid had its driest year in 1963, with grid 19364 at 58% of normal.</p>"}
